=== DESIGN ===

OBJECTIVE
The codec package is the wire-bytes <-> typed-Atomic boundary for the
Tesla Fleet Telemetry pipeline. It owns three responsibilities and
nothing else:

  1. proto.Unmarshal of the outer Payload bytes.
  2. Per-Datum decode via protomodel.DecodeDatum (Prompt 0014).
  3. Compound flattening at the boundary so downstream consumers
     (router, normalize.Pipeline, signal.Store) NEVER observe a nested
     map/struct shape — ADR-004 #4.

PUBLIC API
The package surface is intentionally tiny:

  type Atomic struct {
      Field     string    // canonical signal name OR flatten-derived suffix
      Value     any       // typed primitive (string/bool/int/float/time.Time/typed enum)
      EmittedAt time.Time // Payload.CreatedAt; zero Time if producer omitted
      VehicleID string    // Payload.Vin (NOT internal numeric vehicles.id)
  }

  func Decode(payload []byte) ([]Atomic, error)

Per-compound flatten helpers, the per-datum dispatch, the metric
registrations, and the protobuf Payload type are unexported. The codec
is purely transformational: no Redis, no DB, no MQTT.

DISPATCH
flattenIfCompound switches on the runtime type of the value returned by
DecodeDatum, dispatching as:

  protomodel.Location     -> flattenLocation       (2 atomics: {field}Latitude, {field}Longitude)
  protomodel.Doors        -> flattenDoors          (6 atomics: {field}{DriverFront..TrunkRear})
  protomodel.TireLocation -> flattenTireLocation   (10 atomics: 4 wheels + 6 Semi positions)
  protomodel.Time         -> flattenTime           (1 atomic: time.Time anchored to EmittedAt UTC date)
  string + field=DoorState                  -> flattenDoorStateJSON                   (6 atomics)
  string + field=ScheduledChargingStartTime -> flattenScheduledChargingStartTimeJSON  (1 atomic, time.Time)
  string + field=ScheduledDepartureTime     -> flattenScheduledDepartureTimeJSON      (1 atomic, time.Time)
  default                                   -> single-element pass-through

The four typed compound message variants are returned by the protomodel
decoder for proto Value_LocationValue / Value_DoorValue /
Value_TireLocationValue / Value_TimeValue. The three JSON-shaped
compounds arrive as *string* values whose Datum.Key matches one of the
three compound field names; the codec dispatches on the field name
because the wire shape is indistinguishable from any other string
without that key.

Of the seven SignalMeta entries with IsCompound=true today:
  Location (21), OriginLocation (111), DestinationLocation (112)  -> Location flattener
  TpmsHardWarnings (224), TpmsSoftWarnings (225)                  -> TireLocation flattener
  DoorState (58)                                                  -> DoorState JSON flattener
  ScheduledChargingStartTime (44), ScheduledDepartureTime (46)    -> respective JSON flatteners

No live Field uses Value_DoorValue or Value_TimeValue today, but the
codec covers them defensively because the proto schema permits them and
the protomodel decoder already returns Doors/Time structs for those
oneof variants.

FAILURE SEMANTICS (per ADR-004)
  - Outer proto.Unmarshal failure   -> Decode returns an error.
                                       The MQTT handler may surface
                                       this for redelivery; this is the
                                       ONLY failure that triggers
                                       redelivery per the architecture
                                       document.
  - ErrInvalid (Datum.Value.invalid)-> drop + bump invalid_values_total{field}.
  - ErrUnsetValue (oneof unset)     -> drop + bump unset_values_total{field}.
  - Unhandled DecodeDatum error     -> drop + bump decode_errors_total{field}.
  - JSON parse failure inside one
    of the three string compounds   -> drop + bump flatten_errors_total{field}.
  - Per-Datum errors NEVER abort the surrounding Payload — the
    remaining Data entries are decoded and returned to the caller. A
    single producer bug must NOT trigger redelivery of the entire batch.

CHILD-NAME PREFIXING
Compound child atomics use {sourceFieldName}{ChildName} to disambiguate
the three Location-typed fields (Location/OriginLocation/DestinationLocation)
and the two TireLocation-typed fields (TpmsHardWarnings/TpmsSoftWarnings).
The legacy internal/telemetry/flatten.go used bare "Latitude"/"Longitude"
for Location only, which would collide if multiple Location-shaped fields
ever appeared in the same payload. The new naming is collision-free by
construction.

DOORS vs DOORSTATE NAMING (the prompt's documented decision)
The proto Doors struct uses {DriverFront, DriverRear, PassengerFront,
PassengerRear, TrunkFront, TrunkRear}. The JSON DoorState wire shape
uses {DriverFront, DriverRear, PassengerFront, PassengerRear, FrontTrunk,
RearTrunk} — note the trunk pair is named differently. We preserve both
shapes verbatim in their respective flatteners rather than aliasing one
to the other:
  - flattenDoors         -> ...TrunkFront / ...TrunkRear   (proto names)
  - flattenDoorStateJSON -> DoorStateFrontTrunk / DoorStateRearTrunk (JSON keys)

Production today only emits DoorState as JSON (Field=58 -> string_value
-> flattenDoorStateJSON), so signal_log will only ever see the
FrontTrunk/RearTrunk variants. If a future producer ever switches to
Value_DoorValue for the same field, the divergent names will be
externally observable in signal_log — that is the explicit design
choice. Renaming proto field accessors inside the codec to "match" the
JSON shape would silently corrupt provenance for any operator reading
the schema.

TIME ANCHORING
flattenTime and the two scheduled-time JSON flatteners produce a single
time.Time atomic constructed via time.Date(EmittedAt.Year/Month/Day,
H, M, S, 0, time.UTC). The Hour/Minute/Second is the producer-emitted
clock-time-of-day; the date is the Payload-level CreatedAt's UTC date.
For ScheduledCharging/Departure times, the date is a downstream
rendering convenience and is NOT a claim about the actual scheduled
execution date. If EmittedAt is the zero Time (producer omitted
CreatedAt), we anchor to year 1 UTC so the value is still a sortable
timestamp — clockTimeOnDate handles this branch.

OUT-OF-RANGE Hour/Minute/Second values are normalised by Go's time.Date
(it wraps 25:00:00 to next-day 01:00:00 etc.). We accept the wrap
rather than rejecting the row because the downstream router can already
inspect the value and apply its own validation; dropping here would
leak a producer bug as a missing-row gap rather than a visible
out-of-range timestamp.

VEHICLE_ID FIELD
The Atomic.VehicleID carries the Payload's Vin string verbatim, NOT
the internal vehicles.id numeric primary key. The codec is intentionally
vendor-only; mapping VIN -> internal id happens at the next layer
(router or signal.Store). This keeps the codec free of any database
dependency and decision about how to handle unknown VINs.

METRICS
Four CounterVec metrics under namespace "teslasync", subsystem "codec":
  invalid_values_total{field}  - Datum dropped because Value.invalid=true
  unset_values_total{field}    - Datum dropped because oneof was unset
  decode_errors_total{field}   - Datum dropped due to other DecodeDatum error
  flatten_errors_total{field}  - Datum dropped because per-field flattener failed

All registered via promauto so they auto-publish on /metrics without an
explicit Register call. Label cardinality is bounded by the proto's Field
enum (~260 entries) which is acceptable for Prometheus.

=== UNIT_TEST ===

flatten_test.go covers the per-compound flatten helpers in isolation:

  TestFlattenLocation_FullyPopulated
    - 1 fully-populated Location -> 2 atomics named LocationLatitude/Longitude
    - asserts float64 type on Value, fixedEmittedAt on EmittedAt, fixedVIN on VehicleID

  TestFlattenLocation_FieldNamePrefixDistinguishesSources
    - same Location through "OriginLocation" prefix vs "DestinationLocation"
    - locks in the {fieldName}Lat/Lng convention so a regression that
      reverts to bare "Latitude"/"Longitude" trips the test

  TestFlattenDoors_FullyPopulated
    - 1 fully-populated proto Doors (TrunkFront/TrunkRear) -> 6 atomics
    - asserts each child name + bool round-trip
    - locks in the proto-style {Trunk}{Front,Rear} naming

  TestFlattenTireLocation_FullyPopulated
    - 1 fully-populated TireLocation (10 positions) -> 10 atomics
    - asserts the full set of names including Semi-truck positions
    - asserts a spot-checked child preserves the bool

  TestFlattenTime_FullyPopulated
    - protomodel.Time{14, 25, 33} + fixedEmittedAt -> 1 atomic with
      Value of type time.Time at fixedEmittedAt's date, 14:25:33 UTC

  TestFlattenTime_ZeroEmittedAtFallsBackToEpochYear
    - locks in the year-1 fallback used by clockTimeOnDate when the
      producer omitted CreatedAt — without this the codec would emit a
      year-0 timestamp which TimescaleDB rejects

  TestFlattenDoorStateJSON_FullyPopulated
    - JSON DoorState string -> 6 atomics (FrontTrunk/RearTrunk shape)
    - asserts each child name + bool round-trip

  TestFlattenDoorStateJSON_MalformedReturnsError
    - garbage JSON returns an error (caller drops + counts)

  TestFlattenScheduledChargingStartTimeJSON_FullyPopulated
  TestFlattenScheduledDepartureTimeJSON_FullyPopulated
    - JSON {Hour,Minute,Second} payload -> 1 time.Time atomic at the
      expected clock components, anchored to fixedEmittedAt

  TestFlattenScheduledDepartureTimeJSON_MalformedReturnsError
    - garbage JSON returns an error

codec_test.go covers the bytes-in / atomics-out contract end-to-end:

  TestDecode_MixedPayload
    - one Payload with: a happy float scalar (VehicleSpeed), a happy
      enum (Gear -> ftproto.ShiftState_D), a proto compound
      (Location), a JSON string compound (DoorState), an
      invalid-flagged Datum (BatteryLevel), and an unset-oneof Datum
      (RatedRange).
    - asserts the exact set of 10 output atomic Field names
    - asserts the dropped fields (BatteryLevel, RatedRange) do NOT
      appear in any guise
    - asserts every atomic carries the Payload-level VIN and CreatedAt
    - asserts scalar/enum/Location values preserve their decoded Go type

  TestDecode_AtomicValuesAreFlat
    - reflective enforcement of ADR-004 #4: no Atomic.Value may be of
      type protomodel.Location/Doors/TireLocation/Time/DoorState/
      ScheduledChargingStartTime/ScheduledDepartureTime. Uses reflect
      so a future-added compound type in protomodel/compounds.go
      requires updating the forbidden map but cannot bypass it.

  TestDecode_MalformedBytesError
    - garbage bytes -> Decode returns an error AND nil atoms. This is
      the redelivery contract: only outer Unmarshal failures propagate.

  TestDecode_EmptyPayloadIsEmptySlice
    - Payload with zero Data entries -> empty atom slice, no error

  TestDecode_PerDatumFailuresDoNotAbortPayload
    - Payload with a malformed-JSON DoorState wedged between two valid
      scalars: the JSON parse failure must drop the DoorState row
      WITHOUT aborting the surrounding Payload. Both scalars must
      survive in the output.

  TestFlattenIfCompound_PassThroughForScalar
    - non-compound float32 -> single-element pass-through atomic with
      EmittedAt + VehicleID propagated correctly

  TestFlattenIfCompound_StringNonCompoundFieldIsPassThrough
    - string-typed value whose field is NOT one of the three JSON
      compound fields (e.g. VehicleName) flows through unchanged. Locks
      in the string-vs-JSON dispatch so the codec doesn't accidentally
      JSON-parse arbitrary strings.

